BT /F1 10 Tf 54 729 Td (12.2 Managers. Managers must make sure their teams have read and understood the Code, complete) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 716 Td (training on time and know how to raise concerns. Managers who receive a concern must pass it to) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 703 Td (Legal and Compliance or the Speak Up Officer.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 681 Td (12.3 Training. All new employees must complete Code of Conduct training within 30 days of) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 668 Td (joining. After that, every employee must complete the annual Code of Conduct refresher by 31) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 655 Td (October each year. The refresher is assigned in Keel and covers this Code, anti-bribery, gifts) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 642 Td (and hospitality, competition law and speaking up. Legal and Compliance reports completion rates) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 629 Td (to ExCo monthly during the training window, and the company target is 98% completion by the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 616 Td (deadline. Employees who have not completed the training by the deadline will be reminded by) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 603 Td (their manager, and persistent non-completion may be treated as a disciplinary matter. Employees) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 590 Td (in higher-risk roles, including Sales, Procurement and Trade Compliance, also complete) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 577 Td (role-specific modules.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 555 Td (12.4 Certification. As part of the annual refresher, every employee certifies that they have) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 542 Td (read the Code, that they have complied with it, and that they have reported any breaches of) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 529 Td (which they are aware.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 507 Td (12.5 Investigations. Suspected breaches will be investigated promptly, fairly and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 494 Td (confidentially by people independent of the matter. Employees must cooperate fully with) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 481 Td (investigations and must not destroy or alter relevant documents.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 459 Td (12.6 Consequences. Breaches of the Code may result in disciplinary action up to and including) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 446 Td (dismissal, and may be reported to the relevant authorities. Managers who ignore or fail to) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 433 Td (report breaches may also face disciplinary action.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 411 Td (12.7 Waivers. Waivers of this Code for directors or members of ExCo may only be granted by the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 398 Td (Board. Other waivers may only be granted by the General Counsel, in writing.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 376 Td (12.8 Review. This Code is reviewed at least every three years, or sooner if there are) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 363 Td (significant changes in law or in our business. The next scheduled review is in January 2028.) Tj ET
